["I need to make 24 using 8, 5, 5, 9. Each number used once. Operators +, -, *, /.\n\nLet me try various combinations.\n\nNumbers: 8, 5, 5, 9\n\nLet me think.\n\n8 + 5 + 5 + 9 = 27, too big.\n8 * 5 = 40, 40 - 9 - 5 = 26. No.\n9 * 5 = 45, 45 - 8 - 5 = 32. No.\n\nLet me think about 24.\n\n(9 - 5) = 4, 4 * 5 = 20, 20 + 8 = 28. No.\n(9 - 5) = 4, 4 * 8 = 32, 32 - 5 = 27. No.\n(8 - 5) = 3, 3 * 9 = 27, 27 - 5 = 22. No.\n(8 - 5) = 3, 3 * 5 = 15, 15 + 9 = 24! Yes!\n\nSo (8 - 5) * 5 + 9 = 3 * 5 + 9 = 15 + 9 = 24. \n\nLet me verify: 8, 5, 5, 9 all used once. (8 - 5) * 5 + 9 = 24. Yes!\n"]